        "original_id": "c37773b7-ad63-5b54-82b8-a464d3683233",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich, Germany; Netherlands\n- Companies: Löwenbräu; Anheuser-Busch InBev\n- Buildings: Bürgerbräukeller\n- People: Georg Elser; Adolf Hitler\n- Governments: German Nazi government\n- Events: Venlo Incident; failed assassination attempt; invasion of the Netherlands\n\nFacts:\n- The Bürgerbräukeller was a large beer hall in Munich, Germany.\n- Löwenbräu is a brewery in Munich owned by Anheuser-Busch InBev.\n- On 8 November 1939, Georg Elser carried out a failed assassination attempt on German Chancellor Adolf Hitler at the Bürgerbräukeller in Munich, Germany.\n- The German Nazi government later used the Venlo Incident to link Britain to Georg Elser's failed assassination attempt on Adolf Hitler.\n- The German Nazi government used the Venlo Incident to help justify Germany's invasion of the neutral Netherlands on 10 May 1940.",
